    Fix audio overlap by measuring actual TTS durations and scheduling sequentially
    
    Root cause: Audio segments were delayed with adelay() but not tracked for actual duration.
    When Khmer speech was longer than English, segments would overlap.
    
    Fix implemented:
    1. Measure actual audio durations using FFprobe after TTS generation
    2. Schedule segments sequentially with natural pauses (150ms between, 400ms for speaker changes)
    3. Use adelay() to position each segment at its scheduled start time
    4. Use amix() with duration=longest to include all audio
    5. Preserve original timestamps in segment metadata
    
    Key changes in compose_audio_timeline():
    - _get_audio_duration() measures actual Khmer audio length
    - Sequential scheduling prevents overlap (next segment starts after prev + pause)
    - Natural pauses: 150ms (comma pause), 400ms (paragraph/speaker change)
    - duration=longest ensures all audio is included, not truncated

